  "title": "Models as Tools: An Agentic Coordination Framework for Unified Multimodal Visual Tracking",
  "summary": "arXiv Computer Vision presents a framework called ACTrack, which enables heterogeneous models as invocable tools through event-triggered mechanisms, allowing for the integration of different tools to achieve superior performance in visual tracking. VC-Tooler, another agentic multimodal approach, focuses on learning compositional and adaptive visual tool use across multiple steps and tool contexts.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ACTrack coordinates a Tracker-based Instance Matching Tool, a SAM3 Motion Tool, and a VLM Reprompt Tool for efficient, multi-tool coordination.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "ACTrack achieves state-of-the-art results on eight RGB benchmarks, surpassing the strongest and largest trackers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "VC-Tooler learns visual tool use as a compositional and adaptive capability through a hierarchical synthesis pipeline and reinforcement learning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
